LIVE PROBE DONE 2026-08-24 -- the one probe this ticket asked for. VERDICT: AKI.IO /openai/v1
speaks native OpenAI tool calling. The hermes route is unnecessary.

Request sent through Engine::AKIAnthropic-free path, AKIOpenAI with tool_wire_format overridden
to "openai" (model minimax-m2.5-230b, the docs table lists it as fully supported):

  POST https://aki.io/openai/v1/chat/completions
  {"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"add","description":"Add two numbers",
    "parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"a":{"type":"number"},"b":{"type":"number"}},
    "required":["a","b"]}}}],"tool_choice":"auto", ...}

  <- 200 OK
  "message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning":"The user wants me to add 7 and 15 using the add tool.",
    "tool_calls":[{"id":"call_a4b814fb215b4738a83bed34","type":"function",
      "function":{"name":"add","arguments":"{\"a\": 7, \"b\": 15}"}}]}
  finish_reason: stop

Native tools array accepted, native tool_calls block returned, arguments intact. The docs were
right and the code comment in Engine::AKIOpenAI ("AKI /openai/v1 endpoint does not support
native tool parameters") is stale.

Replayed through chat_response as shipped (tool_wire_format still hermes): tool_calls comes
back correctly populated with id, name and arguments {"a":7,"b":15}. That is not luck --
Role::OpenAICompatible::chat_response deliberately pins the extractor to "openai" regardless
of tool_wire_format (the comment at OpenAICompatible.pm:~355 says so). So the RESPONSE side is
already native-ready; only the REQUEST side still builds the hermes prompt scaffold.

Consequence: switching Engine::AKIOpenAI off Role::HermesTools is a request-side change only.
Expect it to also cut prompt_tokens -- the hermes scaffold is pure prompt overhead the model no
longer needs to be taught.

